-faded\">your main protein source</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">breadcrumbs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for binding and texture</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">piece</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">egg</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">helps hold everything together</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">small</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">onion (minced)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds flavor and moisture</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic (minced)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a kick of taste</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">chili powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">brings the spice</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">paprika</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a bit of smokiness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">cayenne pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">extra heat!</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">to enhance flavors</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a subtle kick</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for cooking the patties</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-7639-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7639\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the patties</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Mixing bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For combining ingredients</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-7639-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-7639-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7639\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7639-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">In a bowl, combine ground chicken, breadcrumbs, egg, onion, garlic, chili powder, paprika, cayenne, salt, and pepper.</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7639-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Mix until everything is evenly combined. Get in there and use your hands if you need to!</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7639-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Form the mixture into 4-6 equal patties. Make them as thick or thin as you like!</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7639-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat. You want it hot but not smoking!</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7639-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Cook the patties for 4-5 minutes per side or until they are golden brown and cooked through. Flip them carefully!</div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7639-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\">Serve hot on buns or with a fresh salad. Enjoy your spicy chicken patties!</div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-7639-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>250</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>12g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s what you’ll need to make these delicious spicy chicken patties!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Spicy-Chicken-Patties.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for spicy chicken patties displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-7637\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Spicy-Chicken-Patties.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Spicy-Chicken-Patties-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 lb ground chicken</strong> – your main protein source</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 cup breadcrumbs</strong> – for binding and texture</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 egg</strong> – helps hold everything together</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 small onion (minced)</strong> – adds flavor and moisture</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cloves garlic (minced)</strong> – for a kick of taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp chili powder</strong> – brings the spice</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 tsp paprika</strong> – for a bit of smokiness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 tsp cayenne pepper</strong> – extra heat!</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 tsp salt</strong> – to enhance flavors</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 tsp black pepper</strong> – adds a subtle kick</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tbsp oil</strong> – for cooking the patties</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-spicy-chicken-patties\"><strong>How to Make Spicy Chicken Patties</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to whip up some delicious spicy chicken patties! With a preparation time of about 15 minutes and a cooking time of 10-12 minutes, you’ll have these juicy delights ready in no time. Let’s get cooking!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Making-Spicy-Chicken-Patties.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making spicy chicken patties, including ingredients, mixing, forming patties, and cooking in a skillet.\" class=\"wp-image-7638\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Making-Spicy-Chicken-Patties.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Making-Spicy-Chicken-Patties-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Combine Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, combine ground chicken, breadcrumbs, egg, onion, garlic, chili powder, paprika, cayenne, salt, and pepper.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Mix Well</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Mix until everything is evenly combined. Get in there and use your hands if you need to!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Form Patties</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Form the mixture into 4-6 equal patties. Make them as thick or thin as you like!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Heat the Skillet</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat. You want it hot but not smoking!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Cook the Patties</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cook the patties for 4-5 minutes per side or until they are golden brown and cooked through. Flip them carefully!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Serve and Enjoy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve hot on buns or with a fresh salad. Enjoy your spicy chicken patties!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>12 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>27 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot on buns or with a fresh salad!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-spicy-chicken-patties\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making spicy chicken patties</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use ground chicken for a juicy texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add finely chopped vegetables for extra flavor and moisture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chill the patties before cooking to help them hold their shape.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with spices to find your perfect heat level.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a cooling dip to balance the spice.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-spicy-chicken-patties\"><strong>How to Serve this spicy chicken patties</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with a zesty avocado salsa for a fresh kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a side of sweet potato fries for a delightful crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with tangy yogurt sauce and fresh herbs for extra flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy in a warm pita with lettuce and tomatoes for a tasty wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside a crisp garden salad for a light meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Make sliders with mini buns for a fun party appetizer.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Accompany with a spicy dipping sauce for an extra zing.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to store your spicy chicken patties for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow patties to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container or wrap tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool patties completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap each <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patty\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">patty </a>in plastic wrap, then place in a freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For best results, reheat in the oven at 350°F (175°C) for 10-15 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, use a skillet over medium heat for 5-7 minutes, flipping occasionally.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ensure patties are heated through to an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C).</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Does Tyson still make spicy chicken patties?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, Tyson continues to produce a variety of chicken products, including spicy chicken patties. You can check their official website or local grocery stores for availability and specific product lines that may include spicy options.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What makes chicken patties spicy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chicken patties can be made spicy through the addition of various spices and seasonings. Common ingredients include cayenne pepper, chili powder, garlic powder, and black pepper, which all contribute to that delightful kick. You can adjust the spice levels according to your taste preferences.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Does Walmart have spicy chicken patties?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, Walmart typically carries a range of frozen and fresh chicken products, including spicy chicken patties. Availability may vary by location, so it’s a good idea to check their website or call your local store to confirm stock.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What are the spices in chicken patties?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The spices in chicken patties can vary widely, but common ones include paprika, cayenne pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, and black pepper. Some recipes may also incorporate herbs like oregano or thyme for added flavor. Feel free to experiment with your favorite spices to create your perfect spicy chicken patty!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to savor the delightful flavors of these spicy chicken patties! They’re not just easy to make, but each bite is a burst of joy that’ll remind you of cozy family gatherings. So, roll up your sleeves, gather your ingredients, and enjoy the simple pleasure of creating something delicious. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
